        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Tin Cup Challenge: Seniors West of the Tetons</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/50880.webp" alt="Tin Cup Challenge: Seniors West of the Tetons" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The Tin Cup Challenge enables Seniors West of the Tetons to enrich the lives of aging adults in Teton Valley through advocacy, diverse programming, and wellness and nutrition opportunities.&nbsp; These unrestricted funds collected through the Community Foundation of Teton Valley allow us to provide health, nutrition and fitness programs as well as fun social activities at the Senior Center, around the community and beyond. Those programs are essential in combating isolation and loneliness that is vital to the wellbeing of older adults.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Don’t just take our word for it.</p>

<p><em>“Each day you wake up you need to have a purpose and SWOT gives purpose to the senior community. Two years ago we were new to the Teton Valley and the Senior Center has allowed us to connect with others. Having community with others is important to keeping our outlook positive. SWOT offers amazing programs and community.” &#8211; Cindie Brouwer</em></p>

<p>“<em>Just received our first delivered meal. I eagerly opened my lunch and immediately started crying. They were tears of joy as I could feel the love from all in Teton Valley. And the food was delicious. Thank you for loving and caring for us.” &#8211; Lina Marquis</em></p>

<p><em>“In a valley of this size, the Senior Center is an incredible gift to the community.” &#8211; Julie Stockdale</em></p>

<p><em>“Friendship, companionship, laughter – that’s what SWOT means to me. &#8211; Jackie McManus</em></p>

<p><em>“I appreciate these meals so much. I’m 92, and I can’t get to the store. It means so much.” &#8211; Alice McIntosh</em></p>
        </div>

